## Agent Stripe Credit Top-Up Endpoints (Not x402)

These legacy mppx paths charge an existing account's saved Stripe payment method and add account API credits. They are path aliases, not an x402 or MPP payment-challenge protocol.

- Credit balance: `GET https://api.builtwith.com/mppx/api-discovery`
- Spending limits: `GET https://api.builtwith.com/mppx/api-configuration`
- Credit purchase: `POST https://api.builtwith.com/mppx/api-purchase` with a unique `Idempotency-Key`; quantities use fixed increments of 2,000.
- Auth: separately scoped Agent Billing Key in `Authorization: Bearer`; general API keys and temporary `bw-` tokens cannot purchase. Monthly limits reset in UTC.
- Local OpenAPI discovery: `GET https://api.builtwith.com/mppx/openapi.json`
- BuiltWith.com aliases:
  - `GET https://builtwith.com/mppx/api-discovery`
  - `GET https://builtwith.com/mppx/api-configuration`
  - `POST https://builtwith.com/mppx/api-purchase`
  - `GET https://builtwith.com/mppx/openapi.json`

## x402 Paid Access

BuiltWith supports accountless x402 v2 access through prepaid MCP lookup units and fixed-price HTTP routes. These lookup units are separate from account API credits.

- Human documentation: `GET https://api.builtwith.com/x402-api`
- Canonical configuration and live pricing: `GET https://api.builtwith.com/.well-known/x402`
- MCP endpoint: `https://api.builtwith.com/mcp`
- Prepaid MCP flow: call `x402-pricing`, purchase at least 2,000 non-expiring lookup units with `x402-credit-purchase`, then pass the returned reusable `creditKey` to an `x402-*` lookup tool. Payment proof is sent in MCP request metadata at `_meta["x402/payment"]` only for purchases.
- One-off HTTP flow: discover the 12 fixed-price API routes and two List-pass purchase routes at `GET https://api.builtwith.com/openapi.json`. Send the intended query/body, read `PAYMENT-REQUIRED`, and retry the identical request with `PAYMENT-SIGNATURE`; successful settlement returns `PAYMENT-RESPONSE`.
- The descriptor is authoritative for the facilitator, network, asset, payment address, available tools, volume tiers, and List passes; clients should not hard-code those values.

